# Risk and Execution

Specs: `docs/context/BROKER_SPEC.md`, `docs/context/OPERATIONS_RUNBOOK.md`.

This is the only path to the broker and the only place that authorizes exposure.

## Orders and capital

- One logical order uses one stable idempotency key across every retry.
- A timeout or acknowledgement never proves a fill.
- Unknown submit outcome blocks replacement until broker reconciliation. Never
  blind-retry.
- Capital is reserved before submission, released only from confirmed events.
- Every open position maps to active deterministic protective coverage.
- Stops only tighten. Widening requires a versioned tested policy.

## Decisions

Input `TradeIntent`, output `APPROVE`, `RESIZE`, `DEFER` or `REJECT`, always
with machine-readable reason codes and a durable decision record. Recalculate
max loss, margin, exposure and executable price here; never trust the
strategy's numbers.

## Reconciliation

Runs on boot, reconnect, schedule, manual request and anomaly. Broker wins.
Classify every difference, repair deterministically, emit a
`ReconciliationEvent`. Entries stay blocked until critical breaks resolve.

## Adapter boundary

The broker adapter translates commands and responses. It holds no strategy
logic, no sizing, no stop policy, no AI call, and no retry policy that can
create duplicate risk.

Verify current broker behavior before coding against it. Never hard-code a
remembered exchange threshold.
